/target
crate/target
*.bak

# Cargo.lock IS committed for the crate: it pins rasn-compiler's version and the
# tool's output depends on it. Regenerate with `cargo build` after changing deps.
!crate/Cargo.lock

# pkg/ is wasm-pack output. It is committed deliberately so the site can be
# deployed without a Rust toolchain present. Regenerate with:
#   cd crate && wasm-pack build --target web --release --out-dir ../web/pkg
!web/pkg/
!web/pkg/**

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node deps. CI runs `npm install --no-save playwright` to drive the button
# audit; that lands here and must never be committed or served. gitignoring the
# directory is what stops a stray install reaching the deployed artifact.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

